<item>
            <title>[BOOKKEEPER-1105] RackAwarePolicy: Failure to map node into rack may result in failure to add other nodes.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/BOOKKEEPER-1105</link>
                <project id="12311293" key="BOOKKEEPER">Bookkeeper</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Ran into this issue:&lt;br/&gt;
due to some misconfiguration of new node and rack assignments we&apos;ve ended up with nodes being assigned to default rack. We are not using region-aware, only rack-aware policy.&lt;br/&gt;
This generates the following sequence of events:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;default rack is /default-region/default-rack even though region-aware is not used.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;other nodes mapped to racks like /rack1, /rack2 etc.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;mixing /region/rack and /rack styles is not allowed, but exception on addition of such nodes is swallowed. All following nodes to add (if there were any) just skipped as result.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
